id: pm-help-required-metadata
title: Declare machine-help requiredness independently of description prose
description: "Machine help currently infers semantic requiredness from description markers in help-json-payload.ts. A concise title-help rewrite during GH1577 kept its meaning but dropped [required], making --help --json report title.required=false; the existing regression caught it before delivery. Keep current compatibility wording for this PR and design explicit metadata as a separate improvement."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,contracts,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-25T01:25:04.612Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T01:25:04.612Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Preserve pm_help_v1 required/value-name semantics and GH441 active-mode behavior; declare semantic requiredness independently of value arity and text; prove shortening or localizing descriptions cannot alter requiredness; keep CLI/SDK/MCP discovery and fixed help budgets aligned.
why_now: "Separate machine contracts from human wording so concise help, wording improvements and future localization cannot silently change agent decisions."
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Requiredness comes from explicit semantic contract and active type/create-mode policy, while human descriptions can change without changing machine metadata."
